   "html_text": "Matthias Steup (2000; 2008; 2012; 2017), a leading proponent of doxastic compatibilism, argues that compatibilism entails that (most of) our actions and our beliefs are free; for similar reasons, he also thinks we can believe intentionally. More specifically, most of our doxastic attitudes fulfill the most popular compatibilist requirements for free action: e.g., they fit with reactive attitudes, fit with our higher-order attitudes, are weakly intentional, and are caused by a reasons-responsive ",
